course: dictionary
lesson: 2630
title: Despair and feelings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Despair means you have lost all hope, so nothing seems like it can get better. Look at the clues around the word: «Then the Mole despairs again: there's nothing to eat, not a crumb!» The Mole has tried, found nothing, and now feels hopeless.
explain: «Inside, the Mole sees dust everywhere, a cold, small, shabby, long-forgotten house — and flops onto a hall-chair in despair.» Dust, cold and a flop onto a chair all show a tired, sad feeling. Despair is that heavy feeling of no hope.
explain: Despair can be a noun, a feeling, or a verb, something you do. Try swapping in «lost all hope» to check your meaning. If the sentence still makes sense, you have got it right.
fact: Despair means the feeling of having lost all hope.
fact: As a verb, «despair» means to lose hope: «Don't despair — we'll find your cat.»
fact: «Drive someone to despair» means make them feel hopeless and worried.
fact: Despair is often the low point in a story, just before things change.
fact: If you feel hopeless, talk to someone you trust, such as a family member, friend or teacher.
exercise: What does «despair» mean? | Being tired after a long walk | Feeling very excited about a day out | *The feeling of having lost all hope
exercise: In «flops onto a hall-chair in despair», what does despair suggest about the Mole? | Excited about his new home | He wants to go outside and play | *He has lost all hope | He is very hungry
exercise: Nadia says despair is just a fancy word for sad. What is the better answer? | Despair means exactly the same as sad, so there is no difference at all | *Despair is stronger: it means you have lost all hope | Despair means happy and full of energy
test: «Drive someone to despair» means what? | Make someone very happy | *Make someone feel hopeless and worried | Play a game with someone | Help someone with their homework
test: Which sentence uses despair as a verb? | *«Don't despair — we'll find your cat.» | The despair of the cold house | The Mole sat in despair | A house full of dust
exam: If you feel hopeless, what should you do? | Wait until the feeling goes away by itself | Keep it secret forever | *Talk to someone you trust | Stop eating and sleeping
